	(text "STOP/PRESENCE DRAFT: loop powered only by P3V3; external NC stop contact returns STOP_SEND to STOP_RETURN. No external voltage.\nMain connector presence requires a passive link on C between PRESENCE_OUT and PRESENCE_RETURN. Open loop disarms.\nCTRL_ALIVE must come from supervised controller reset/power status. All three inputs have receiver pull-downs.\nContact wetting, cable capacitance, ESD/EMC and complete worst-case Schmitt thresholds remain to qualify before release.\nNo certified STO or short-to-supply detection is claimed. The independent brake must not be disabled by this stop path."
		(at 660 795 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7f937434-1bda-48b6-92f9-04bae6a629f0")
	)
	(text "WATCHDOG DRAFT: both transition polarities count. U631/U632 give 128 us nominal retriggerable coverage; U633 ORs them.\nU636/U637 generate 27.04 us short windows. Each detector flip-flop samples the opposite-edge window.\nWD_OK requires recent activity and no early-edge indication. Accepted interval allocation changes to 30-100 us, nominal 50 us.\nFault retention/acknowledgement is implemented on faults.kicad_sch. Propagation/setup/hold, startup and component-corner validation remain pending. See watchdog document."
		(at 35 810 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dbd954eb-0fc3-417d-8369-93f43a6104eb")
	)
	(text "INCOMPLETE INTERLOCK: ARM_FAULTS_OK and WAKE_FAULTS_OK now come from the retained-fault sheet; raw protection sources remain pending.\nNo bridging these signals for normal operation. Main connector and brake/OC/OV/thermal qualification remain pending. Retained acknowledgement is on faults.kicad_sch.\nQ sets only on an ARM_REQ rising edge while ARM_READY is high; ARM_READY low asynchronously clears Q and directly masks PWM.\nMOTOR_PERMISSION = Q AND ARM_REQ AND ARM_READY. Wake permission is separate so SPI setup can occur with all PWM masked.\nC_DRV_WAKE_REQ uses provisional interface contact 47, replacing reserved SYNC/CNV. All local logic uses P3V3."
		(at 35 555 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b1041db0-3988-4770-b5a3-4e78ecc0579c")
	)
	(text "WAKE_READY = RAILS_OK AND WAKE_CONDITIONS_OK AND (NOT ARM_REQ OR WD_OK).\nA watchdog fault during ARM_REQ removes both driver ENABLE and PWM permission. ARM_REQ low permits diagnostic/configuration wake.\nWAKE_CONDITIONS_OK = STOP_OK AND PRESENCE_OK AND CTRL_ALIVE_OK AND WAKE_FAULTS_OK from the retained-fault sheet.\nARM_CORE_READY = WD_OK AND ARM_FAULTS_OK; retained fault acknowledgement is on faults.kicad_sch; CORE/WAKE_PROTECTIONS_OK remain pending."
		(at 35 580 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a867454c-a9fe-4f1d-aa13-d341c1ef5625")
	)
